{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T13:42:01.566236", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # We will first check if the item is a primitive and if it is present in the environment. If yes then we will collect it.\n  if item in env.world.cookbook.primitives:\n    actions = collect(env, item)\n    return actions\n  # If the item is not a primitive, we will check if the recipe for the item exists in the cookbook.\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item)\n  if recipe is None:\n    return []\n  # We will then check if the required ingredients for the recipe are present in the inventory.\n  required_ingredients = {}\n  for ingredient, count in recipe.items():\n    if ingredient != \"_key\":\n      required_ingredients[ingredient] = count\n  for ingredient, count in required_ingredients.items():\n    if env._current_state.inventory[ingredient] < count:\n      return []\n  # We will now move to the workshop specified in the recipe.\n  workshop = recipe[\"_key\"]\n  workshop_pos = find_workshop(env, workshop)\n  if workshop_pos is None:\n    return []\n  # We will then move to the workshop and perform the USE action to craft the item.\n  actions = move_to(env, workshop_pos)\n  actions.append(env.action_specs()[USE])\n  return actions", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
