{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T15:19:19.296805", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  # get the index of the item in the cookbook index\n  index = env._current_state.world.cookbook.index\n  # item_id = index.index(item)  # index is a function, not an attribute\n  item_id = index(item)\n  # get the recipe for the item\n  recipe = env._current_state.world.cookbook.recipes.get(item_id, {})\n  if not recipe:\n      return []\n  # check if we have all the required items in the inventory\n  inventory = env._current_state.inventory\n  required_items = {k: v for k, v in recipe.items() if k != '_key'}\n  for required_item_id, required_count in required_items.items():\n      if inventory[required_item_id] < required_count:\n          return []\n  # get the workshop for the item\n  workshop_id = recipe['_key']\n  # get the position of the workshop\n  grid = env._current_state.grid\n  workshop_pos = None\n  for i in range(grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(grid.shape[1]):\n          if grid[i, j, workshop_id] == 1:\n              workshop_pos = (i, j)\n              break\n      if workshop_pos:\n          break\n  if not workshop_pos:\n      return []\n  # move to the workshop\n  current_pos = env._current_state.pos\n  # move to the workshop\n  # calculate the direction to the workshop\n  dx = workshop_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n  dy = workshop_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n  # move in the direction\n  # this is a very simple movement logic, in reality you would need a more complex path finding algorithm\n  for _ in range(abs(dx)):\n      if dx > 0:\n          actions.append(env.action_specs()['DOWN'])\n      else:\n          actions.append(env.action_specs()['UP'])\n  for _ in range(abs(dy)):\n      if dy > 0:\n          actions.append(env.action_specs()['RIGHT'])\n      else:\n          actions.append(env.action_specs()['LEFT'])\n  # use the workshop\n  actions.append(env.action_specs()['USE'])\n  return actions", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-09-12T15:19:22.100154", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  def collect_needed_items(craft_item, needed_items):\n    \"\"\"Recursively collect all items needed for the given item. The function is called with the item to be crafted and returns all the items needed to craft it. It uses the primitive_for function from the cookbook to get the required items for the given item. It then recursively calls itself for each of those items to get their required items. The function returns a list of all the items needed to craft the given item.\"\"\"\n    # Use the primitive_for function to get the required items for the given item\n    required_items = env._current_state.scenario.world.cookbook.primitive_for(craft_item)\n    # Check if the required items are already in the needed_items list\n    for required_item in required_items:\n      if required_item not in needed_items:\n        # If not, add it to the list and recursively collect its required items\n        needed_items.append(required_item)\n        collect_needed_items(required_item, needed_items)\n    return needed_items\n\n  def collect_all_items(needed_items, collected_items):\n    \"\"\"Collects all the needed items. The function is called with the list of needed items and the list of collected items. It checks if the agent has all the needed items in its inventory. If not, it calls the collect function for each of the missing items and appends the actions to the collected_items list. The function returns the list of actions to collect all the needed items.\"\"\"\n    # Check if the agent has all the needed items in its inventory\n    for needed_item in needed_items:\n      if env._current_state.inventory[needed_item] == 0:\n        # If not, collect the item and append the actions to the collected_items list\n        collected_actions = collect(needed_item)\n        collected_items.extend(collected_actions)\n    return collected_items\n\n  def get_workshop_location(craft_item):\n    \"\"\"Gets the workshop location for the given item. The function is called with the item to be crafted and returns the workshop location. It uses the recipes from the cookbook to get the workshop location for the given item. The function returns the workshop location as a tuple of (x, y) coordinates.\"\"\"\n    # Use the recipes from the cookbook to get the workshop location for the given item\n    workshop_location = env._current_state.scenario.world.cookbook.recipes[craft_item][\"workshop\"]\n    # Return the workshop location as a tuple of (x, y) coordinates\n    return workshop_location\n\n  def move_to_workshop(workshop_location):\n    \"\"\"Moves the agent to the workshop location. The function is called with the workshop location and returns the list of actions to move to the workshop. It uses the move function to move the agent to the workshop location. The function returns the list of actions to move to the workshop.\"\"\"\n    # Use the move function to move the agent to the workshop location\n    actions = move(workshop_location)\n    # Return the list of actions to move to the workshop\n    return actions\n\n  def craft_item_at_workshop(craft_item):\n    \"\"\"Crafts the item at the workshop. The function is called with the item to be crafted and returns the list of actions to craft the item. It uses the craft function to craft the item at the workshop. The function returns the list of actions to craft the item.\"\"\"\n    # Use the craft function to craft the item at the workshop\n    actions = craft(craft_item)\n    # Return the list of actions to craft the item\n    return actions\n\n  # Get the index of the item to be crafted\n  craft_item_index = env.world.cookbook.index.index(item)\n  # Collect all the needed items\n  needed_items = collect_needed_items(craft_item_index, [])\n  collected_items = collect_all_items(needed_items, [])\n  # Get the workshop location for the item to be crafted\n  workshop_location = get_workshop_location(craft_item_index)\n  # Move to the workshop location\n  move_actions = move_to_workshop(workshop_location)\n  # Craft the item at the workshop\n  craft_actions = craft_item_at_workshop(craft_item_index)\n  # Return the list of actions to collect all the needed items, move to the workshop, and craft the item\n  return collected_items + move_actions + craft_actions", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
